This bug is real, and makes shopping free for the majority of shops.
I'm sure the dev team will fix it next release, so don't read further
if you want to look forward to new releases of nethack...






















Next time you are in a shop, look around for the most expensive item
(try standing over an item and #chat with the shopkeeper, he'll quote
a price).  Pick it up, and throw it down to the floor.  Now the fun
begins...he'll pay you for it, not at the rate he quoted you, but
at his cost (which is actually good enough, considering the 
circumstances).  As if this wasn't good enough, he'll pay you
not just once, but twice!  Think the shopkeeper will wisen up after
you have taken advantage of him?  Think again.  Pick up the same
item, throw it down.  He pays you again, twice!  Imagine the
possibilities... 

Now you can walk into a shop zorkmid-less and walk out with all
the goods, making out like a bandit, without any of the consequences 
you've grown to know and fear.  It's all legal and does not piss off 
the shopkeeper or your god in any way.

You shouldn't have read this.  Once you get used to shopping this
way you'll never go back.  The dev team WILL fix this (I didn't
discover the bug myself, ran across it in this news group a while
ago, so they must know), and sometime down the road you'll have to 
choose to not upgrade, or go through withdrawl.  But, for now enjoy.

One thing you should be aware of though...

The dev team, even when it screws up leaving a hole like this,
has an equalizer...segmentation faults (or whatever your system does 
when the program crashes).  

Make sure you are playing a version with checkpointing turned on 
to save your game as you enter every level.  If you see a message to 
the effect "error in shopkeeper administration", you may leave the
shop, but you might not leave the level intact.

Make sure you have a version of recover handy to restore your game 
when this happens.  If you don't, you should save and back up your 
game before you begin shopping.   

MORALITY

I had a certain moral dilemma for a time when I started shopping
this way (I know it's just a game, but I felt guilty about cheating
it), but after I thought about it I realized it was just another
(unplanned) feature of the game.  

I know the dev team will probably cringe at having a major bug referred 
to in this fashion, but in the overall scheme of the nethack universe, 
I like the fact that even the dev team gods can't control everything.  

Somehow all those aggrevating deaths (staying asleep while monsters 
are pound away at me until I die, or meeting a monster carrying a 
wand of death) seem to melt away, when I now enter a huge scroll
shop, or (on those rare occasions) find an artifact in a weapons shop 
for 12 zillion zorkmids.  

I have deliberately not described all the aspects of this new
way of shopping, some good, some bad...in the true nethack tradition 
I'll leave them for you to discover.  

For the record, I play nethack 3.1.0 compiled for Sun Unix.  I 
don't know if this bug has been fixed in 3.1.1, or even if it
exists in other versions of 3.1.0.  

Shop til you drop,

